We're looking for a Senior Operational Accountant, Contracts &amp; Revenue , to join our Subsidy team and help manage the accounting behind our fast-growing state subsidy program. In this role, you'll turn subsidy contract terms into accurate revenue, billing, and reporting across multiple states. Reporting to the Team Lead, Accounting Management - State Subsidies, you'll partner with Accounting, Finance, Operations, and state agencies to keep results accurate and on time.

About the Role

• Interpret state operating and capital subsidy contracts into accounting treatment and billing requirements.

• Build the route-level subsidy bus miles forecast and revenue budget and explain variances to budget and prior year.

• Own the monthly subsidy P&amp;L, revenue amortization, and month-end close, with supporting reconciliations and journal entries.

• Maintain the monthly subsidy reconciliation database, keeping it balanced to the general ledger.

• Manage the full invoice process for your assigned states, from preparation to submission, and follow up on receivables.

• Oversee state-funded bus accounting, including depreciation and dispositions, with Fixed Assets and Operations.

• Support annual audits and present subsidy results to leadership.

About You

• Bachelor's degree in Accounting.

• 5+ years of experience in complex accounting, including journal entries, reconciliations, budgeting and forecasting.

• Strong knowledge of GAAP and general ledger accounting, with experience in revenue contracts and fixed assets.

• Experience with government grant or subsidy accounting preferred.

• Advanced Excel and PowerPoint skills and ERP experience (NetSuite or similar); Power BI or Access a plus.

• Detail oriented and comfortable with dense contract language, with strong analytical skills.

• Clear communicator who can manage multiple state contracts and deadlines and work with leadership and state agencies.

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Comprehensive Wellness Coverage - Competitive Medical, Vision, and Dental plans, including multiple FSAs (Health and Dependent Care).&nbsp; &nbsp;

• 401(k) Matching - 401(k) plan with up to 4% company matching contributions.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Flexible Time Off - Take time off when you need it, as you need it, subject to business needs and manager approval.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Paid Parental Leave - 8 week s of fully paid leave to support new parents and growing families.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Company Paid Life Insurance - Basic company-paid life insurance equal to your annual salary.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Lifestyle Spending Account - Receive up to $600 per year for eligible lifestyle-related services.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Tuition Support - Up to $5,250 per year reimbursed for your continued education and development after 12 months of continuous service.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• 24/7 Employee Assistance Program - Free, confidential support for mental health, legal, financial, and family issues, including up to 5 free counseling sessions per year.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere - Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp; &nbsp;

